Z||000000||REDHOTT88||11-28-2001||03:20 PM||||I haven't seen any Fieros with white lettering on the tires... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Is this a no-no?  I have blackwalls on my 88 Formula, but was considering having Goodyear, etc. tires installed with the white lettering showing.<P>Any pix, feedback?<P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR>1988 Formula 2.8L V6 <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (red & shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||11-28-2001||03:23 PM||||I am not sure the stock tires had white letters or not, but when I bought my Formula it had Goodyear GT+4's with outlined white lettering on them.  That was the stock type of tire if I am not mistaken.  I thought they looked fine.  I always liked white letter tires, but there aren't too many left... unless you own an SUV.  I think they would look fine on your Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000002||SS_304||11-28-2001||03:36 PM||||Firestone Firehawk tires on a Fiero would look great.||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||11-28-2001||03:36 PM||||Thanks Formula88 & SS_304 !!<P>I'd like to see some pix!! I wonder if the white letters would look too "busy" on a such a small car..     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Anyone? Bueller?<P><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||REDHOTT88||11-28-2001||04:40 PM||||<BR>Anyone got pix?||||reg||1
Z||000005||RRobinson||11-28-2001||05:01 PM||||Blackwall Eagle GTs were standard on all 86-87 GTs with diamond spoke wheels.<P>Blackwall Eagle GT+4s were standard on all 88 Formulas and GTs.<P>OWL Eagle GTs were optional on 84-87 SEs and 85 GTs, as well as standard on the Indy (I think). They may have also been available on Sport Coupe models.<P>My opinion? Love 'em with the notchback and hi tech wheels. No with diamond spoke wheels. No no no on 88 Formulas and GTs. Just my opinion.<P>RR<BR>2-88 GTs<BR>2-87 GTs<BR>87 SE V6 5-Speed<BR>86 GT 5-Speed<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ferrari_cdn||11-28-2001||06:02 PM||||I have white lettering on my tires.  When I purchased my white '84, the front two tires had a faded out outlined white letter saying TURBO LAZER 4 and the rear ones with solid BFGOODWRENCH(sp?) RADIAL T/A<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">   </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||1
