Z||000019||Raydar||11-28-2001||08:50 PM||||When I bought my GT in 85, I saw quite a few Fieros with outline white letter tires. Were fairly common. Mine just had the blackwalls, though. <BR>Do what you feel like.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Fformula88||11-28-2001||09:12 PM||||Redhott... yeah, they were only on the back.  The front tires were so badly dry rotted that I got the dealer I bought it from to throw in new front tires.  They put on blackwalls so I drove around with a mix for a while!<P>I liked it, but I didn't want to spend for the Goodyears when I bought new tires so I got a set od blackwall Dunlops.  The white letters look fine with the black rims IMO, but I am happy with what I have too.<P>I am now running Dunlop SP Sport A2's on the back (front has some older D60 A2's).  The new SP Sports have a highly detailed sidewall, and looks very good all shined up.  Either way I am sure the car would look great!<P>PS, Same Fiero?  Nice choice in Fiero's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000021||FieroHarry||11-28-2001||09:57 PM||||Here's my "non"placing Fiero at the 2001 Nationals next to Tweeties <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>To me a Fiero without RWL's is like a Fiero without a wing.<P>Just doesnt seem natural   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/harrynats_2.jpg">  <BR>Not to mention there fun to see in relfections of the sides of other cars pulling away from them at stop lights   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>------------------<P><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B><P>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 11-28-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||6
